# Do not materialise optional peer dependencies into this repo's lockfile.
#
# The library declares 18 optional peers so consumers can pick a provider or a
# store, but it imports none of them: every integration goes through an
# interface, and even the bundled reference adapters are structurally typed.
# With pnpm's default `auto-install-peers=true`, all 18 were installed as direct
# dependencies of the workspace root — dragging in nodemailer, mjml (and its
# unmaintained html-minifier), twilio, firebase-admin and the AWS SDKs, none of
# which any source, test or script touches.
#
# That surface produced every open Dependabot alert on this repository, for code
# that is never executed here and is never published (the package ships
# `dependencies: {}`). The required peers are declared as devDependencies, so
# they stay installed and the gates keep running against them.
auto-install-peers=false
